SCOPE AND UPSTREAM RIGHTS
-------------------------
This licence covers the *derived* tables produced by the analysis code in
this repository (data/derived/, data/processed/, data/reference/).

It does not and cannot relicense the primary data they are derived from.
Those remain under the terms of their original publications:

  data/raw/feng2022/        KRAS G12C saturation mutagenesis atlas
                            Feng et al. 2022
  data/raw/oh2026/          ALK prime-editing resistance atlas
                            Oh et al. 2026
  data/raw/met_estevam2024/ MET kinase-domain deep mutational scan
                            Estevam et al. 2024, doi:10.1101/2024.07.16.603579
  MET screen hit lists      Transcribed from Supplementary Tables S1 and S2
                            of Tiedt et al. 2011
  Mutagen spectra           Arnold et al. 2012 (germline ENU compilation);
                            Doi et al. 2022 supplementary NGS (Mutazyme II)

Anyone reusing data/raw/ should consult and cite those sources directly.
Each derived table carries back-references to the record it came from, and
data/derived/CHECKSUMS.sha256 fixes the version used for the manuscript.

NOT DISTRIBUTED
---------------
Patient-level clinical records (data/raw/harmonized_cohort/patients.csv,
mutations.csv, treatment_lines.csv) are not included in this repository.
They derive in part from AACR Project GENIE, GENIE BPC, MSK-IMPACT and
MSK-CHORD, whose data use agreements do not permit redistribution, and they
carry demographics and survival for 612 individuals. Nothing in the analysis
reads them; the manuscript's derived tables reproduce byte for byte without
them. Their schema is documented in data/raw/harmonized_cohort/README.md.
